.vscode-test/**
# The bare names too, not just their contents. A parallel worktree symlinks both
# of these at the root checkout's copies (a 400MB editor download and
# node_modules), and `<name>/**` matches what is INSIDE a directory — never a
# symlink that merely bears the name. Without these two lines `vsce package`
# from a worktree bundles the symlinks and secretlint dies reading one as a file
# (`EISDIR`). Same trailing-slash trap `.gitignore` had for `.vscode-test`.
.vscode-test
